# Read by autoprefixer (postcss.config.js) to decide which vendor
# prefixes/fallbacks a given CSS property actually needs. Brave uses the
# same Chromium engine as Chrome, so it isn't listed separately here —
# targeting "Chrome" already covers it exactly, since Brave doesn't fork
# the rendering engine, only the browser chrome/features around it.
#
# Safari/iOS get an explicit version floor (>= 14, ~2020) rather than
# "last N versions" — that keyword only enumerates recent point releases
# (e.g. resolved to Safari 26.1-26.4 only, all from the same year, in
# testing), which is correct for someone fully updated but silently drops
# prefixes/fallbacks a real person on an older, no-longer-updatable
# iPhone would still need — exactly the "any kind of browser" case this
# is meant to cover. The other browsers auto-update aggressively enough
# that "last 4 versions" already gives a realistic, current spread.
last 4 Chrome versions
last 4 ChromeAndroid versions
last 4 Edge versions
last 4 Firefox versions
last 4 FirefoxAndroid versions
last 4 Samsung versions
Safari >= 14
iOS >= 14
not dead
